A.1.140. {"problem": "The diff sets status to 'proposed' on the handoff, on request_delivery and on the DeliveryRequest object. The post-change files show all three as 'confirmed'. The new interview refs (authoring L40, delivery L27) carry no quote, and the change request gives no reason. So a confirmation for the new branch behaviour is claimed without evidence, or the diff and the files disagree about the status.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml handoffs.deliver_approved_commit; delivery.domain.yaml actions.request_delivery and objects.DeliveryRequest (source/status)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.1.141. {"problem": "The request says Delivery should refuse requests that do not say which branch. Nothing does that. The branch param is only a required type, with no precondition or invariant. Delivery never uses the branch: preview, deploy and run_probes do not pass it to the kernel, and no rule checks it. The description sentence 'The request must say which branch' is not enforced. Delivery 'knows' the branch only as an unused field.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml actions.request_delivery, preview, deploy, run_probes; invariants", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.1.142. {"problem": "Adding a required param to request_delivery changes the interface the handoff targets as '1.x', and the composition wires interface 1. Neither the delivery version (8) nor the interface version is shown as bumped. Existing 1.x callers that omit branch would now be refused, and the fixtures still carry interface 1.0.0 requests.", "where": "toprope-self.composition.yaml wiring/members; authoring handoffs.deliver_approved_commit to.interface 1.x; delivery.domain.yaml version", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
