A.2.140. {"problem": "The new required `branch` param on `request_delivery` is a breaking change to the Delivery interface that Authoring hands off to (`interface: 1.x`, composition `interface: 1`). Neither version is bumped (authoring 20, delivery 8, composition 1), and the fixtures stay at interface 1.0.0 and 1.x. Any caller or in-flight request that omits `branch` is now refused, so the old behaviour changes without a new interface version.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml actions.request_delivery; authoring.domain.yaml handoffs.deliver_approved_commit; toprope-self.composition.yaml members/wiring", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.2.141. {"problem": "The `branch` fixtures conflict with the domain's own model. The description says `branch` is the branch the commit came from, but every DeliveryRequest fixture uses `branch: main`. Authoring's real commits are on branch `work`, and approval merges them into main. The glossary says a commit reaches main only by approval. So the handoff will send `work` while the fixtures and scenarios model `main`, which misrepresents the data.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml world.fixtures R1-R6 `branch: main`; authoring.domain.yaml world Commit C1-C3 `branch: work`", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
A.2.142. {"problem": "`branch` is required and carried on DeliveryRequest, but nothing uses it. The deploy floor glossary says 'on main', yet `preview`, `deploy` and `run_probes` only pass domain and commit to the kernel, and no precondition or invariant checks the branch. The request is 'refused if it does not say', but the stated purpose (Delivery knowing the origin branch) has no effect, and a request naming a non-main branch is not treated any differently.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml DeliveryRequest.branch, actions preview/deploy/run_probes, glossary 'deploy floor'", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.2.143. {"problem": "Provenance and status are inconsistent. The diff marks the DeliveryRequest object, `request_delivery` and the handoff as `proposed`, but the files after the change show them as `confirmed`. The earlier confirming interview quotes were dropped, and the sources were repointed to L27 (delivery) and L40 (authoring), with no quote. DeliveryRequest's original source L20 is also still cited by the scenario `deliver-preview-deploy-verify`. A confirmed element that rests on no recorded owner confirmation of the branch requirement, and that is not what the diff says, should not be deployed.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml objects.DeliveryRequest and actions.request_delivery source/status; authoring.domain.yaml handoffs.deliver_approved_commit source/status", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.2.144. {"problem": "The `refuse requests that do not say` requirement is not covered by any scenario. No scenario exercises a `request_delivery` with a missing `branch`, and the existing scenarios start from fixtures, so the refusal behaviour is untested.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml scenarios", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
