A.3.140. {"problem": "The change request has no stated reason, and the new behaviour has no confirming evidence. Both source refs were moved to new interview lines (authoring L40, delivery L27) and the quote was dropped. The diff marks the elements 'proposed', but the post-change files show the handoff, the DeliveryRequest object and request_delivery as 'confirmed'. Nothing confirmed by a person backs a change to a permission-adjacent handoff. The DeliveryRequest object was also re-sourced to L27 and the request_delivery action to L27, with no quote at either place.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml handoffs.deliver_approved_commit; delivery.domain.yaml objects.DeliveryRequest and actions.request_delivery (source/status)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.3.141. {"problem": "The new required `branch` param on request_delivery is a breaking change to the interface Authoring hands to Delivery. The composition still pins interface 1 and the handoff targets '1.x'. Neither domain's version (authoring 20, delivery 8) was bumped. Any older sender, or one whose handoff was not updated, would be refused or would break.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml version / request_delivery; toprope-self.composition.yaml members and wiring; authoring handoff interface 1.x", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.3.142. {"problem": "The 'refuse requests that do not say' part is not enforced. `branch` is a plain required string, and no precondition or invariant refuses an empty or missing value. The description sentence is the only statement of the rule. Nothing uses branch afterwards either: the preview, deploy and probe calls pass only domain and commit. The deploy floor ('on main') is untouched, so the field is recorded and never acted on.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml actions.request_delivery, DeliveryRequest.branch, deploy/preview effects", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.3.143. {"problem": "The delivery fixtures R1–R6 all say branch: main. The authoring commits they stand for (C1–C3) are on branch 'work', and the handoff sends target.branch, so the real value would be 'work'. The fixtures therefore misstate what the handoff delivers. The glossary says only commits on main are delivered, which makes the meaning of 'the branch the commit came from' unclear.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml world.fixtures R1–R6; authoring.domain.yaml world Commit fixtures and glossary 'main'", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
A.3.144. {"problem": "The delivery glossary entry 'delivery request' and the DeliveryRequest description do not mention the branch. The object description still reads as a request to deliver an approved commit, with no branch.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml glossary 'delivery request', objects.DeliveryRequest.description", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
