A.4.140. {"problem": "The change request says delivery should refuse requests that do not name a branch, but nothing refuses them. branch is only a required string param on request_delivery. No precondition or invariant rejects an empty branch value, and no action ever reads or checks branch. preview, deploy and probe still pass only domain and commit to the kernel, so the branch has no effect on delivery.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml, actions.request_delivery and DeliveryRequest.branch", "kind": "behaviour", "from": "llm"}
A.4.141. {"problem": "The branch value handed over is the commit's own branch, and the existing commits are on 'work' (C1, C2 and C3 in the authoring world). The delivery fixtures R1 to R6 all set branch: main. The glossary says only commits on main are delivered, and the deploy floor requires 'on main'. A real handoff would therefore send 'work' while delivery's examples and rules assume 'main'. It is unclear whether branch means the origin branch or main, and the fixtures hide the mismatch.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml handoffs.deliver_approved_commit (branch: target.branch) vs delivery.domain.yaml world fixtures and glossary 'deploy floor'", "kind": "contradiction", "from": "llm"}
A.4.142. {"problem": "Adding a required param to request_delivery is a breaking change to the interface. The composition still pins interface 1 and the handoff targets '1.x', and the fixtures stay at 1.0.0 and 1.1.0. Any caller of the old shape would now fail, and the version numbers do not signal the break.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml actions.request_delivery; toprope-self.composition.yaml members/wiring; authoring handoff 'interface: 1.x'", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.4.143. {"problem": "The diff flips already-confirmed elements to status: proposed (the authoring handoff, DeliveryRequest and request_delivery) and drops the confirming interview quote. It replaces that quote with new refs (authoring interview L40, delivery interview L27) that carry no quote. The previous confirmation of the handoff (the 20/21 agreement) is lost, and the new refs are not backed by a recorded person's agreement. The delivered 'after' files also show these elements as confirmed, so the diff and the resulting files disagree on their status. The change request gives no 'Why'.", "where": "authoring.domain.yaml handoffs.deliver_approved_commit; delivery.domain.yaml objects.DeliveryRequest and actions.request_delivery (source/status)", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
A.4.144. {"problem": "The delivery interview ref for DeliveryRequest and request_delivery was changed to L27. The authoring DecisionRequest object already cites authoring interview L27 for a different topic. The scenario deliver-preview-deploy-verify still cites delivery interview L20, which was the old DeliveryRequest ref. The provenance is inconsistent and does not clearly support the new branch requirement.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml objects.DeliveryRequest source, scenarios.deliver-preview-deploy-verify source", "kind": "reference", "from": "llm"}
A.4.145. {"problem": "The description of request_delivery and the glossary entry 'delivery request' do not say what the branch is for. No scenario covers a request without a branch being refused.", "where": "delivery.domain.yaml glossary 'delivery request'; scenarios", "kind": "other", "from": "llm"}
